# The Lion-Turtle: "can't ... block unless there are three or more Lesson cards in your graveyard" (CR 509.1b). Bot1 has two Lessons
# (Octopus Forms cast with Mox Sapphire's {U} and the Turtle's own "{T}: Add one mana of any color") when Bot2's Memnite attacks on
# turn 4: the block is refused (Bot1 takes 1, 23 -> 22). A third Form, cast at instant speed with the Turtle's mana, makes three,
# and on turn 6 the Turtle blocks the Memnite and kills it (the positive control; the Island is Bot2's hand-size discard).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
The Lion-Turtle
Octopus Form
Octopus Form
Octopus Form
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.The Lion-Turtle.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Octopus Form.Cast(The Lion-Turtle)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.The Lion-Turtle.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Octopus Form.Cast(The Lion-Turtle)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(The Lion-Turtle > Memnite)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Lion-Turtle.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Octopus Form.Cast(The Lion-Turtle)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 22
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(The Lion-Turtle > Memnite)
[T6 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite; Island
Bot1.Life = 22
